  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN265.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">piriviṭai vēṟupaṭṭa talaimaka ḷāṟṟāmai mītūrat tōḻikkuc colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What SHE, who had undergone changes in the time of separation, said to the confidante when [her] lack of strength was increasing.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN265.1">
        <l><anchor n="1"/>pukaiyiṟ poṅkiya viyalvicum pukantu</l>
        <l>paṉiyū raḻaṟkoṭi kaṭup<supplied>pa</supplied>t tōṉṟu</l>
        <l>mimaiyac cevvarai māṉuṅ kollō</l>
        <l>pulampukaḻ niṟainta velpōr tantar </l>
        <l>cīrmiku pāṭaliṟ kuḻīik kaṅkai</l>
        <l>nīrmutaṟ karanta nitiyaṅ kol<supplied>lō</supplied></l>
        <l>ve<supplied>va</supplied>ṉkol vā<supplied>ḻi</supplied> tōḻi vayaṅkoḷi</l>
        <l>niḻaṟpā laṟali ṉeṟitta kūntaṟ</l>
        <l>kuḻaṟkuraṟ pāvai yiraṅka nattuṟan</l>
        <l>toṇṭo<supplied>ṭi</supplied> nekiḻac cāayc cellaloṭu</l>
        <l>kaṇpaṉi kaluḻntiyā moḻiyap poṟaiyaṭain</l>
        <l>tiṉcilai yeḻilēṟu keṇṭip puraiya</l>
        <l>niṇampoti viḻuttaṭi ne<supplied>ru</supplied>ppiṉ <anchor n="2"/>vaitteṭut</l>
        <l>taṇaṅkaru marapiṟ pēe<supplied>y</supplied> pōla</l>
        <l>viḷarūṉ ṟiṉṟa vēṭkai nīṅkat</l>
        <l>tukaḷaṟa virainta tōppi <supplied>pa</supplied>rukik</l>
        <l>kulāa valviṟ koṭunōk kāṭavar</l>
        <l><anchor n="3"/>pulāak kaiyuram pūcā vāya</l>
        <l>rorā<supplied>a</supplied> vuruṭṭuṅ kuṭumik kurāloṭu</l>
        <l>marāañ cīṟūr maruṅkiṟ ṟūṅkuñ</l>
        <l>cennutal <supplied>yā</supplied>ṉai vēṅkaṭan <anchor n="4"/>taḻī<supplied>i</supplied></l>
        <l>vemmuṉai yaruñcura miṟantōr</l>
        <l>nammiṉum vali<supplied>tā</supplied>t tūkkiya poruḷē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="3">Does it resemble the red mountains of the Himalaya</l>
        <l corresp="2">that appear like fiery creepers spread with dew,</l>
        <l corresp="1">ascending into the wide sky with [clouds] churning like smoke?</l>
        <l corresp="6">Is it a treasure hidden in the water</l>
        <l corresp="5">of the Gaṅgā, accumulating because of the excellent singing</l>
        <l corresp="4">of those who brought [it], of victorious battle copious in fame on the field?</l>
        <l corresp="7a-c">What is it, oh friend?</l>
        <l corresp="23">– the wealth that is weighed as stronger than us</l>
        <l corresp="9">by the one who abandoned us so that the girl  grieves with [her] flute voice,</l>
        <l corresp="7d-8">[her] tresses curled like black sand in the shade of shining brightness,</l>
        <l>while we stay behind, becoming emaciated so that [our] bright bangles</l>
        <l corresp="10-11c">become loose, [our] eyes weeping tears with distress,</l>
        <l corresp="22">the one who traversed the difficult desert with hot frontiers,</l>
        <l corresp="21">hugging the Vēṅkaṭam [mountain] with elephants with red foreheads,</l>
        <l>where, after having reached the height, having cut up the graceful bull with a sweet bellow</l>
        <l corresp="11d-13">having put to the fire the excellent pieces covered with fat that are superb,</l>
        <l corresp="14">[and], like demonesses according to [their] frightful difficult custom,</l>
        <l corresp="15">when the desire to eat the cooked meat left [them],</l>
        <l corresp="16">having drunk Tōppi licquor that was fragrant [and] free of dust,</l>
        <l corresp="17">the men with curved strong bows [and] cruel glances,</l>
        <l corresp="18">their strong mouths besmeared by [their] meat-reeking hands,</l>
        <l corresp="20">sway, by the side of the little village with Kadamba trees,</l>
        <l corresp="19">[in turn] with the crested owl that rotates [its head] without stopping.</l>
      </lg>
